[{"category":"section","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms","page":"Welcome","text":"Documentation for PrototypesCriticisms.\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms"},{"category":"method","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.check_kernelmatrix-Tuple{AbstractMatrix{<:Real}}","page":"Welcome","text":"check_kernelmatrix(K)\n\nCheck that the matrix K is square and symmetric, and return the number of observations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.check_kernelmatrix"},{"category":"function","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.criticisms","page":"Welcome","text":"criticisms(x, k, protos, c=1)\ncriticisms(X, k, protos, c=1)\ncriticisms(K, protos, c=1)\n\nCompute criticisms following the MMD-critic method and return their indices.\n\nThe data x, X, or K and the kernel k are as in prototypes_criticisms.\n\nThe remaining arguments are:\n\nprotos::AbstractVector{Int}: the prototypes, e.g., as returned by prototypes.\nc::Int: the number of criticisms to compute.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.criticisms"},{"category":"method","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.importances-Tuple{Vector{Int64}, Matrix{Int64}}","page":"Welcome","text":"importances(observed_ranking, rankings)\n\nCompute the importances for every data instance.\n\nArguments\n\nobserved_ranking::Vector{Int}: the originally observed ranking.\nrankings::Matrix{Int}: the rankings per data feature.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.importances"},{"category":"method","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.importances-Tuple{Vector{Int64}, Vector{Int64}}","page":"Welcome","text":"importances(observed_ranking, ranking)\n\nLike importances, but provide a single ranking for one data feature only.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.importances"},{"category":"method","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.importances-Tuple{Vector{Int64}, Vector{Vector{Int64}}}","page":"Welcome","text":"importances(observed_ranking, rankings)\n\nLike importances, but provide a vector of rankings instead of a matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.importances"},{"category":"function","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.mmd2","page":"Welcome","text":"mmd2(x, k, protos)\nmmd2(X, k, protos)\nmmd2(K, protos)\n\nCompute the squared maximum mean discrepancy (MMD) between the data and prototypes.\n\nThe data x, X, or K and the kernel k are as in prototypes_criticisms.\n\nThe remaining argument is:\n\nprotos::AbstractVector{Int}: the prototypes, e.g., as returned by prototypes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.mmd2"},{"category":"function","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes","page":"Welcome","text":"prototypes(x, k, p=1)\nprototypes(X, k, p=1)\nprototypes(K, p=1)\n\nCompute prototypes following the MMD-critic method and return their indices.\n\nThe data x, X, or K and the kernel k are as in prototypes_criticisms.\n\nThe remaining argument is:\n\np::Int: the number of prototypes to compute, with 1 <= p <= n for n observations.\n\nSee also criticisms.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes"},{"category":"function","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes_criticisms","page":"Welcome","text":"prototypes_criticisms(x, k, p=1, c=1)\nprototypes_criticisms(X, k, p=1, c=1)\nprototypes_criticisms(K, p=1, c=1)\n\nCompute prototypes and criticisms following the MMD-critic method and return a tuple of the indices of the prototypes and the indices of the criticisms.\n\nThe data can be given in the following forms:\n\nx::AbstractVector: a vector of observations, e.g., a vector of vectors or a vector of   numbers for one-dimensional data.\nX::AbstractMatrix{<:Real}: a data matrix, with one observation per column.\nK::AbstractMatrix{<:Real}: a precomputed kernel matrix. Only squareness and symmetry are   checked.\n\nFor x and X, the kernel matrix is computed with the kernel function k.\n\nThe numbers of prototypes p and criticisms c are passed on to prototypes and criticisms.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes_criticisms"},{"category":"method","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes_criticisms-Tuple{Vector{Int64}, AbstractMatrix, Int64, Distances.PreMetric}","page":"Welcome","text":"prototypes_criticisms(observed_ranking::Vector{Int}, D::Matrix, k::Int)\n\nFind prototypes and criticisms based on the clustering of the ranking.\n\nArguments\n\nobserved_ranking::Vector{Int}: the observed ranking.\nD::AbstractMatrix: the data instances.\nk::Int: the number of clusters to find.\nmetric::Distances.PreMetric: the distance metric for computing the distances between the data instances.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes_criticisms"},{"category":"method","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes_criticisms-Tuple{Vector{Int64}, AbstractMatrix, Int64}","page":"Welcome","text":"Like prototypes_criticisms, but provide a pre-computed distance matrix instead of a matrix of data instances and a distance metric.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes_criticisms"},{"category":"method","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes_criticisms-Tuple{Vector{Int64}, Matrix{Int64}, Int64, Int64}","page":"Welcome","text":"prototypes_criticisms(observed_ranking, rankings, p, c)\n\nFind prototypes and criticisms based on the data feature importances.\n\nArguments\n\nobserved_ranking::Vector{Int}: the observed ranking.\nrankings::Matrix{Int}: the rankings per data feature.\np::Int: the number of protoypes to find.\nc::Int: the number of criticisms to find.\n\nNotes\n\nEach ranking contains the data instance identifiers, i.e., every ranking is a mapping of indices to data instances, e.g., observed_ranking[3] = \"data instance at rank 3\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes_criticisms"},{"category":"method","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes_criticisms-Tuple{Vector{Int64}, Vector{Vector{Int64}}, Int64, Int64}","page":"Welcome","text":"prototypes_criticisms(observed_ranking, rankings, p, c)\n\nLike prototypes_criticisms, but provide a vector of rankings instead of a matrix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.prototypes_criticisms"},{"category":"function","location":"#PrototypesCriticisms.witness","page":"Welcome","text":"witness(x, k, protos)\nwitness(X, k, protos)\nwitness(K, protos)\n\nCompute the witness function for every observation.\n\nThe data x, X, or K and the kernel k are as in prototypes_criticisms.\n\nThe remaining argument is:\n\nprotos::AbstractVector{Int}: the prototypes, e.g., as returned by prototypes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"PrototypesCriticisms.witness"}]
